# Copy this file to `.env` and edit. Read at BUILD time by vite.config.ts.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SITE_BASE — the public path the built site is served from.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Every asset URL in every generated .html file is written with this prefix.
# It must match where the files actually end up on the server. If it does not,
# the browser requests the stylesheet from the wrong place, gets a 404, and the
# page renders as unstyled HTML — the single most common cause of "my upload
# has no styling".
#
# Rules: must start with "/" AND end with "/". The build fails fast otherwise.
#
#   Served at                              SITE_BASE
#   -------------------------------------  ------------
#   https://staging-v1.stantonkingdom.com/ /
#   https://stantonkingdom.com/            /
#   https://stantonkingdom.com/staging/    /staging/
#   https://stantonkingdom.com/preview/v2/ /preview/v2/
#
# Rule of thumb: whatever follows the domain in the URL that loads the home
# page, that is your SITE_BASE. Nothing after the domain means just "/".
#
# Change this and rebuild — do NOT hand-edit paths in the built files.

SITE_BASE=/
